<section class="page-header">
<div class="container">
<p style="margin-bottom:8px;"><a href="/blog/" style="color:rgba(255,255,255,0.7);font-size:0.9rem;text-decoration:none;">&larr; Back to Blog</a></p>
<h1>Deer Season Rental: Getting the Whole Crew to Camp</h1>
<p>The nine-day gun season opens the Saturday before Thanksgiving. Here's how to get the crew and the gear to camp.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section class="section">
<div class="container">
<div style="max-width:800px;margin:0 auto;">
<p>In Jackson County, opening weekend of the gun deer season is practically a holiday. This year the nine-day season opens the Saturday before Thanksgiving &mdash; <strong>November 21</strong> &mdash; and that means camps filling up across the Black River State Forest and the county's public and private land. If your crew is coming in from out of town, or your truck is already spoken for, here's how renters handle the logistics.</p>
<h2>One van for the whole camp</h2>
<p>When five or six hunters are converging from Madison, the Twin Cities, or the Fox Valley, the <a href="15-passenger-van-rental-cost-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">15-passenger van</a> ($135/day + $0.10/mile, $750/week unlimited) gets everyone to camp together with room for bags, coolers, and blaze orange. A full nine-day stretch is where the weekly rate earns its keep.</p>
<p>Smaller group? The <a href="7-passenger-minivan-rental-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">7-passenger minivan</a> ($450/week unlimited) handles a crew of four with gear.</p>
<h2>AWD for the back roads</h2>
<p>The last mile to camp is usually the hard one: gravel, two-tracks, and November slop. Our <a href="/suv-rental.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">SUV &amp; AWD class</a> &mdash; the all-wheel-drive Subaru Outback and two Ford Edge SUVs &mdash; runs $80&ndash;$100/day or $480&ndash;$600/week. Ask for the Outback specifically if AWD matters; there's one.</p>
<h2>Before you load up</h2>
<ul>
<li><strong>Firearms:</strong> transport cased and unloaded, per Wisconsin law &mdash; same as your own vehicle.</li>
<li><strong>Game stays out of the rental:</strong> harvested deer and other game can't be transported in our rental vehicles &mdash; no exceptions. Plan on a camp truck, trailer, or a processor pickup to get your deer out of the woods.</li>
<li><strong>Mud:</strong> it happens. Knock the worst of it off boots and gear &mdash; we appreciate it.</li>
</ul>
<h2>Book early &mdash; really</h2>
<p>Opener week lands right before Thanksgiving, so hunters and holiday travelers are chasing the same vehicles. The van and the AWD Outback are usually the first to go. If your camp dates are set, call now.</p>
<p>Car out of commission after a deer strike? We work <a href="insurance-replacement-rental-cars-black-river-falls.html" style="color:var(--navy);font-weight:600;">insurance replacement rentals</a> with adjusters all season. <strong>Call or text 715-396-1466.</strong></p>
<div style="margin-top:48px;">
<h2>Frequently Asked Questions</h2>
<div class="faq-list">
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">When does the 2026 Wisconsin gun deer season open?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>The nine-day gun deer season opens the Saturday before Thanksgiving, November 21, 2026. Check the Wisconsin DNR for full regulations.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can I rent a van for deer camp?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Our 15-passenger van is $135/day plus $0.10/mile or $750/week with unlimited miles, which covers a full nine-day season.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Do you rent AWD vehicles for hunting trips?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>Yes. Our SUV/AWD class includes an all-wheel-drive Subaru Outback and two Ford Edge SUVs, $80&ndash;$100/day or $480&ndash;$600/week.</p></div>
</div>
<div class="faq-item">
<button class="faq-question" aria-expanded="false">Can I haul a harvested deer in a rental?
<svg xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2000/svg" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><line x1="12" y1="5" x2="12" y2="19"/><line x1="5" y1="12" x2="19" y2="12"/></svg>
</button>
<div class="faq-answer"><p>No. Harvested deer and other game can't be transported in our rental vehicles. Plan on a camp truck, trailer, or processor pickup for your deer.</p></div>
</div>
</div>
</div>
